<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/infographic-fnb-ai-map.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@600;700&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<div class="n3l-fnb-map">
<figure class="fig">

  <header class="mast">
    <span class="eyebrow brand-eyebrow">NEXT3LABS &mdash; F&amp;B operations</span>
    <h1>Where AI goes in a <span class="hi">restaurant</span> group</h1>
    <p class="sub">6 back-office jobs. 3 lanes. The lane decides the order.</p>
    <div class="mast-rule"></div>
  </header>

  <div class="lanes-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">The suitability map</span>
    <span class="legend"><i class="chip chip--go" aria-hidden="true"></i> start now
      &nbsp;<i class="chip chip--mid" aria-hidden="true"></i> behind a person
      &nbsp;<i class="chip chip--stop" aria-hidden="true"></i> not yet</span>
  </div>

  <ol class="lanes">

    <li class="lane lane--go">
      <div class="lane-head">
        <span class="lane-tag">Lane 1</span>
        <h2>Hand over now</h2>
        <p class="lane-why">An error costs an apology, not a customer.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="jobs">
        <li class="job"><h3>Review &amp; enquiry first drafts</h3><p>AI drafts in the brand's voice; a manager reads and posts.</p></li>
        <li class="job"><h3>Invoice vs delivery-note matching</h3><p>Only the mismatches get read. The 11pm job shrinks.</p></li>
        <li class="job"><h3>Prep forecast from sales history</h3><p>A defensible starting count; the head chef still adjusts.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li class="lane lane--mid">
      <div class="lane-head">
        <span class="lane-tag">Lane 2</span>
        <h2>Behind a human checkpoint</h2>
        <p class="lane-why">Useful drafts, real consequences &mdash; a person approves every time.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="jobs">
        <li class="job"><h3>Rostering suggestions</h3><p>A draft roster the outlet manager owns and edits.</p></li>
        <li class="job"><h3>Supplier ordering</h3><p>Draft order, human approval &mdash; orders commit money.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </li>

    <li class="lane lane--stop">
      <div class="lane-head">
        <span class="lane-tag">Lane 3</span>
        <h2>Not yet</h2>
        <p class="lane-why">The blast radius of an error is a penalty, not an apology.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="jobs">
        <li class="job"><h3>Payroll</h3><p>Regulated, precise, unforgiving &mdash; a checking layer at most.</p></li>
        <li class="job"><h3>Regulatory filings</h3><p>Same shape. Keep it with the accountant.</p></li>
        <li class="job"><h3>Customer-facing auto-decisions</h3><p>Auto-replies to complaints, auto-compensation: no person, no.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </li>

  </ol>

  <section class="rules">
    <span class="eyebrow rules-label">The one rule</span>
    <ul class="rule-list">
      <li class="rule-item">An AI error should cost an apology &mdash; not a penalty, a resignation or a customer</li>
      <li class="rule-item">Lane 2 until the track record says otherwise</li>
      <li class="rule-item">The sort comes before the tool</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <figcaption class="foot">
    <span class="verdict"><b class="num">1</b> sorted process in production</span>
    <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
    <span class="verdict">beats any <b class="num">5</b> demos</span>
    <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
    <span class="verdict twist">the lane is the strategy</span>
  </figcaption>

</figure>
</div>